{"company":{"ticker":"SCCO","name":"Southern Copper","sector":"Materials","industry":"Copper","size":"large","cik":1001838},"scores":{"growth":86.0,"quality":68.0,"value":44.0,"acceleration":92.0,"price_momentum":84.0,"reality":82.0,"pricing":69.0},"strategist":{"ticker":"SCCO","opportunity_score":61.0,"components":{"structural_trend":51.0,"capital_flow":46.0,"acceleration":92.0,"quality":68.0,"valuation":44.0,"estimate_revisions":null,"management_commentary":null,"narrative_acceleration":null,"insider_institutional":null},"weights":{"structural_trend":0.2,"capital_flow":0.1,"acceleration":0.15,"quality":0.15,"valuation":0.15,"estimate_revisions":0.1,"management_commentary":0.05,"narrative_acceleration":0.05,"insider_institutional":0.05},"coverage":0.75,"unavailable":{"estimate_revisions":"Estimate-revision feed (Phase 2)","management_commentary":"Earnings Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","narrative_acceleration":"Narrative Intelligence Engine (Phase 2)","insider_institutional":"Form 4 / 13F ingestion (Phase 2)"},"reality":69.0,"narrative":56.0,"pricing":66.0,"expectations_gap":3.0,"macro_fit":55.0,"sector_rotation":-82.0,"theme_pricing":60.0,"checks":[{"label":"Revenue accelerating","ok":true,"evidence":"TTM growth +32.8% vs +21.7% prior quarter"},{"label":"FCF improving","ok":true,"evidence":"FCF growth +47.3%, FCF margin +32.3%"},{"label":"ROIC expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"ROIC +44.0%, incremental ROIC +344.2%"},{"label":"Margins expanding","ok":true,"evidence":"Operating margin +56.9% (+744 bps YoY)"},{"label":"Theme exposure strengthening","ok":false,"evidence":"Exposure-weighted theme trend 51.0"},{"label":"Capital rotating toward sector","ok":false,"evidence":"Materials rotation score -82"},{"label":"Valuation below own history","ok":false,"evidence":"Cheapness vs 5y history 52.0/100"},{"label":"Valuation below sector peers","ok":false,"evidence":"Sector-relative value score 44.0"},{"label":"Balance sheet strong","ok":true,"evidence":"Net debt/EBITDA 0.1"},{"label":"Not diluting shareholders","ok":true,"evidence":"Diluted share count +0.1% YoY"},{"label":"Analyst estimates moving higher","ok":null,"evidence":"Estimate-revision feed not connected (Phase 2)"},{"label":"Management guidance increasing","ok":null,"evidence":"Earnings Intelligence Engine not built (Phase 2)"}],"thesis":"Southern Copper (SCCO) screens at opportunity 61.0 with an expectations gap of 3.0. Reality 69.0 reflects +32.8% TTM revenue growth, +56.9% operating margin and +44.0% ROIC; pricing 66.0 reflects a rich multiple and strong price momentum. Primary theme exposure: Copper & Transition Metals (trend 52.0). Macro fit for Materials in a Goldilocks regime is 55.0/100.","market_expectation":{"summary":"Priced roughly in line with its own history and peers; the market expects the current trajectory to continue.","evidence":["EV/Sales 10.7x (70.0th pct of own 5y range)","P/E 30x (37.0th pct of own history)","FCF yield 3.0%","PEG 0.5","12m return +81%, -8% from 52w high"]},"what_market_misses":["No clear expectations gap: the market appears to have priced what the fundamentals show."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report (roughly 90 days after the last filing on 2026-07-31)"],"risks":["No engine-flagged risks; standard execution and macro risk apply."],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 23% (currently 32.8%)","ROIC falls below 33% (currently 44.0%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200 bps YoY (currently 56.9%)","Materials rotation score turns below -20 for two consecutive runs (currently -82)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55%","Price closes >10% below its 200-day average with negative relative strength","Copper & Transition Metals theme trend drops below 45"],"break_rules":[{"id":"revenue_growth","label":"TTM revenue growth","metric":"revenue_growth","op":"<","threshold":0.2296,"current":0.328},{"id":"roic","label":"ROIC","metric":"roic","op":"<","threshold":0.3298,"current":0.4397},{"id":"margin","label":"Operating margin change YoY","metric":"operating_margin_change","op":"<","threshold":-0.02,"current":0.0743568671985873},{"id":"rotation","label":"Materials rotation score","metric":"sector_rotation","op":"<","threshold":-20,"consecutive":2,"current":-82.0},{"id":"regime","label":"P(Stagflation)+P(Contraction)","metric":"adverse_regime_prob","op":">","threshold":55,"current":48.599999999999994},{"id":"trend","label":"Distance from 200dma","metric":"dist_200dma","op":"<","threshold":-10,"and_negative_rs":true,"current":10.6},{"id":"theme","label":"Copper & Transition Metals theme trend","metric":"theme_trend","theme_id":"copper-electrification","op":"<","threshold":45,"current":52.0}],"narrative_note":"Narrative from the last 7 morning briefs' theme signals (exposure-weighted).","llm_enriched":true,"theme_exposures":[{"theme_id":"copper-electrification","theme":"Copper & Transition Metals","weight":0.8,"order":1,"effective":0.8},{"theme_id":"gold-hard-assets","theme":"Gold & Hard Assets","weight":0.2,"order":2,"effective":0.12}],"llm":{"thesis":"Southern Copper is a best-in-class, low-cost copper asset printing peak-cycle economics: TTM revenue +32.8% and accelerating (from +21.7%), operating margin 56.9% (+744bps YoY), ROIC 44% with incremental ROIC far above it, and FCF up 47% on a 32% FCF margin, all on a near-debt-free balance sheet (net debt/EBITDA 0.07x). The interesting tension is inside the valuation itself: EV/Sales sits at the 70th percentile of its own 5-year range while P/E sits at the 37th and P/FCF at the 30th - the market is paying up for the revenue base but explicitly refusing to capitalize today's margins, i.e. it is underwriting mean reversion in copper prices and mine grades. That is a defensible prior, but it is a bet against persistence, and the engine's expectations gap of just 3.0 means there is no free lunch here - the edge, if any, is duration of the margin regime, not a mispriced fact pattern. Capital flow is the clearest headwind: Materials screens at -82 on rotation versus Technology at +73, meaning the stock's +81% twelve-month return has been delivered without sector flow support, which is both a sign of genuine commodity-driven earnings power and a vulnerability if the marginal buyer never shows up. Net: a high-quality compounder trading roughly at fair value where the asymmetry is copper-price-dependent, not company-specific - size it as a commodity beta expression with an unusually strong balance sheet, not as an alpha idea.","fundamental_read":"This is among the highest-quality P&Ls in Materials: 63.8% gross, 56.9% operating and 36.0% net margins, ROE 45%, ROA 23.5%, with FCF conversion of 90% and capex of only $1.64B against $6.74B of operating cash flow. Net debt of $0.66B against $9.87B EBITDA gives essentially zero financial risk and full optionality on capital allocation; $3.02B of dividends is roughly 59% of FCF, leaving real slack. The caution is that margin expansion of 744bps YoY and incremental ROIC of 344% are price-driven arithmetic, not a structural step-change in cost position - the same operating leverage reverses violently on a copper price break. The 36.3% effective tax rate and low reinvestment rate also mean growth is metal-price growth, not volume growth.","technical_read":"Trend is intact but cooling: price $201.94 sits above a rising 50-day ($194.60) and 200-day ($182.61) in a clean golden-cross configuration, +10.6% above the 200-day, but 8.1% off the 52-week high with -5.7% one-month return. RSI 53 is neutral and MACD histogram is negative, consistent with a digestion phase after +81% over twelve months rather than a distribution top. The $194-195 50-day and the $182 200-day are the levels that matter; a close more than 10% below the 200-day with negative relative strength is the engine's own break trigger.","market_expectation":"At 29.7x earnings, 17.1x EV/EBITDA, 10.7x EV/Sales and a 3.0% FCF yield, the market is paying a premium multiple on sales but a below-median multiple on earnings and cash flow - the textbook signature of a commodity producer at what investors believe is a cyclical earnings peak. Consensus is effectively saying: current copper prices and 57% operating margins are not the run rate, so capitalize them at a discount. The PEG of 0.53 is a statistical artifact of that same mismatch, not evidence of cheapness. With Materials rotation at -82, positioning implies the market expects flows to stay in Technology and treats copper strength as a trade, not a regime.","what_market_misses":["The P/E percentile (37th) versus EV/Sales percentile (70th) divergence is doing real work: the market is discounting the margin, not the asset. If copper's tightness persists even two more years than assumed, the earnings multiple re-rates without the stock needing a higher copper price.","Capex of $1.64B against $6.74B operating cash flow is a 24% reinvestment rate - SCCO is harvesting, not building. Applied across the industry, that underinvestment is itself the bull case for the copper price the market refuses to capitalize.","The balance sheet (0.07x net leverage, $7.3B cash) is not priced as an option. In a commodity drawdown, SCCO is a buyer of distressed assets while leveraged peers are sellers - an asymmetry no multiple currently reflects.","The regime read is effectively noise (Goldilocks 26.3%, Reflation 25.1%, Stagflation 23.7%, Contraction 24.9%) yet Materials rotation is a decisive -82. The market is positioning with conviction against a macro backdrop that carries none - that is crowding, not information.","Price has compounded +81% over twelve months while sector flows were maximally negative, implying the move is fundamentals-driven rather than flow-driven, which historically is the more durable kind."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly report roughly 90 days after the 2026-07-31 filing - the key test is whether revenue growth holds above the 23% break level and margins hold 56%+","Copper price action: any sustained move that re-rates the forward earnings base, since 100% of the margin expansion is price-driven","Dividend declaration cadence - $3.02B paid against $5.10B FCF leaves room for an increase or a special, a direct signal on management's own cycle view","Materials sector rotation score mean-reverting from -82; a turn toward neutral would add flow support to an already-intact price trend","Theme trend on Copper & Transition Metals (currently 52.0, weight 0.80) breaking above 55 would confirm the electrification narrative is re-accelerating"],"risks":["Commodity price beta is the whole thesis: 57% operating margins mean a modest copper decline compresses EPS non-linearly and the 29.7x P/E becomes a trap","Jurisdictional concentration in Peru and Mexico carries permitting, royalty/tax and community-opposition risk that is not visible in any of the supplied financial metrics","Controlled-company structure (Grupo Mexico majority) means minority shareholders do not set capital allocation policy","Materials rotation at -82 versus Technology +73 - if flows stay absent, multiple expansion is unlikely regardless of results","EV/Sales at the 70th percentile of its own history leaves no valuation cushion if growth decelerates from the current +32.8%","Effective tax rate of 36.3% is high and politically sensitive in both operating jurisdictions","Low reinvestment (capex 24% of OCF) implies limited organic volume growth - the story is entirely price, and grade decline is a slow structural drag"],"thesis_break_conditions":["TTM revenue growth falls below 23% (currently 32.8%)","Operating margin compresses more than 200bps YoY from 56.9%","ROIC falls below 33% (currently 44.0%)","P/E percentile rises above ~70th of own history while earnings growth decelerates - i.e. the multiple re-rates for the wrong reason","Net debt/EBITDA rises above 1.0x, signalling either a large acquisition or a cash-flow collapse","Price closes more than 10% below the 200-day ($182.61) with negative relative strength","Copper & Transition Metals theme trend drops below 45","Dividends exceed FCF for two consecutive periods (currently $3.02B vs $5.10B)","Adverse regime (Stagflation + Contraction) probability exceeds 55% (currently 48.6%)"],"second_order_beneficiaries":["Mining equipment and autonomous-haulage vendors: SCCO's grade decline means more tonnes moved per pound of copper, which is a volume tailwind for haul trucks, crushers, grinding media and fleet automation regardless of the copper price","Mining services, engineering and EPC contractors: the industry-wide underinvestment implied by SCCO's 24% reinvestment rate eventually reverses into a capex cycle that these firms monetize first","Water treatment and desalination providers: arid-region copper mining in Peru and northern Mexico is water-constrained, and permitting increasingly hinges on non-freshwater supply","Copper scrap and secondary-recovery processors: if primary supply stays capital-starved, recycled cathode captures incremental demand at structurally better margins","Royalty and streaming companies: they capture commodity upside with none of the jurisdictional capex and community-relations burden that constrains SCCO directly","Grid, cable and transformer manufacturers are the inverse trade - they bear SCCO's pricing power as input cost, and their margin compression is the mirror image of SCCO's 744bps expansion"],"epistemic_labels":[{"statement":"TTM revenue grew 32.8%, accelerating from 21.7% in the prior quarter","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Operating margin is 56.9%, up 744bps YoY; ROIC is 44.0%; FCF margin 32.3% with FCF up 47.3%","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Net debt/EBITDA is 0.07x with $7.33B cash against $7.99B debt","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"P/E 29.7x sits at the 37th percentile of its own 5-year history while EV/Sales 10.7x sits at the 70th percentile","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Materials rotation score is -82, the second-worst of eleven sectors; Technology is +73","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"Price is $201.94, above a rising 50-day and 200-day, 8.1% off the 52-week high, RSI 53, MACD histogram negative","kind":"observed_fact"},{"statement":"The market expects current copper-driven margins to mean-revert and therefore applies a below-median earnings multiple","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"Consensus treats copper strength as a cyclical trade rather than a structural regime, given negative sector flows alongside strong price performance","kind":"consensus_expectation"},{"statement":"The gap between a 70th-percentile EV/Sales and a 37th-percentile P/E is the market discounting margin persistence rather than the asset base","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Capex at only 24% of operating cash flow indicates a harvest posture rather than a growth investment cycle","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Near-uniform regime probabilities (26.3/25.1/23.7/24.9) mean the macro signal carries little information, so the -82 Materials rotation reflects positioning/crowding more than macro conviction","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"A +81% twelve-month return achieved despite maximally negative sector flows suggests fundamentals-driven rather than flow-driven performance","kind":"ai_inference"},{"statement":"Industry-wide underinvestment in new copper supply will extend the tight-market regime beyond what the current earnings multiple discounts","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"The zero-leverage balance sheet becomes a countercyclical acquisition option in a commodity drawdown, an optionality not reflected in the current multiple","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"Peru and Mexico permitting, royalty and community-opposition risk is a material overhang on the growth pipeline","kind":"speculative_hypothesis"},{"statement":"A reversal of the -82 Materials rotation score toward neutral would be sufficient to drive multiple expansion without any change in cop